# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors and operating systems. This working copy lives in a OneDrive
# folder, which writes desktop.ini into directories it syncs.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Virtual environments
.venv/

# Secrets. transcribe.py reads OPENAI_API_KEY from the environment and no key
# is written down anywhere -- these patterns are here to keep it that way.
# Streamlit's secrets file is listed because app.py would make it the obvious
# place to put one.
.env
.env.*
.streamlit/secrets.toml
secrets.json
*.pem
*.key

# Run outputs and recordings. A run is local evidence, not source, and the
# audio is a recording of someone's voice. Both stay out by default.
runs/*
*.wav

# One exception: the run the Block 9 experiments are computed from. Without it
# a clone holds the figures and the CER numbers but nothing to recompute them
# from, so neither can be checked. Data only -- report.json and attempts.jsonl
# are all either script reads. The audio stays local, so the CONTEXT §4 replay
# gate still needs this machine.
!runs/20260927-130613/
runs/20260927-130613/*
!runs/20260927-130613/attempts.jsonl
!runs/20260927-130613/report.json
!runs/20260927-130613/report.md

# The VAD side experiment's outputs, including its two probe clips. The
# *.wav rule above is there because a recording is someone's voice; these
# two are not. They are digital silence and seeded gaussian noise that
# vad_compare.py generates itself (write_probes, seed 20260927), and what
# each side transcribes from them -- "You" without VAD, nothing with it --
# is one of the results. Keeping the exact inputs means that result can be
# checked without regenerating them.
!data/processed/vad_compare/
!data/processed/vad_compare/*.wav
